Add position-based context checkpoints (--checkpoint-pos-step N).

For hybrid/recurrent models the recurrent state only retains its trailing
n_rs_seq positions, so on a partial-prefix divergence the server needs a
context checkpoint at or before the divergence point. Checkpoints are only
created at user-turn starts and the prompt end, so any divergence in the
middle of a long prompt falls back to a full re-prefill.

This adds a --checkpoint-pos-step N flag that also breaks the prompt batch
every N tokens so a checkpoint is created there, letting a diverging slot
reuse a checkpoint within N tokens instead of re-prefilling from zero. The
checkpoint state lives in the RAM prompt cache, not VRAM, so context size
is unaffected. When enabled, checkpoint eviction spacing follows the
position step (not the larger user-turn min-step) so the dense checkpoints
survive.
---
diff --git a/common/arg.cpp b/common/arg.cpp
index 86f8610..e217eed 100644
--- a/common/arg.cpp
+++ b/common/arg.cpp
@@ -1701,6 +1701,16 @@ common_params_context common_params_parser_init(common_params & params, llama_ex
             params.checkpoint_min_step = value;
         }
     ).set_env("LLAMA_ARG_CHECKPOINT_MIN_SPACING_NT").set_examples({LLAMA_EXAMPLE_SERVER}));
+    add_opt(common_arg(
+        {"--checkpoint-pos-step"}, "N",
+        string_format("create a context checkpoint every N tokens (position-based; default: %d, 0 = off)", params.checkpoint_pos_step),
+        [](common_params & params, int value) {
+            if (value < 0) {
+                throw std::invalid_argument("checkpoint-pos-step must be non-negative");
+            }
+            params.checkpoint_pos_step = value;
+        }
+    ).set_env("LLAMA_ARG_CHECKPOINT_POS_STEP").set_examples({LLAMA_EXAMPLE_SERVER}));
     add_opt(common_arg(
         {"-cram", "--cache-ram"}, "N",
         string_format("set the maximum cache size in MiB (default: %d, -1 - no limit, 0 - disable)"
